Maestro.py: 
class for manipulating servos using maestro

mechanism_servo: 
This Python script controls a set of servos using a Pololu Maestro servo controller. It defines two groups of servos (ServoBot1 and ServoBot2) with predefined movement positions.
Features:
	Initialize servos to their default positions.
	Move a specific servo to a target position.
	Move all servos in a group to predefined positions.
	Close the connection to the controller when finished.








Mechanism_1:
 Functionality
Methods:

🏗 lift_planks(): Moves the forklift motor to lift planks and updates the load_type parameter.

🤖 ready_to_pickup(): Positions the servos to pick up objects.#not used

🥫 hold_cans(): Adjusts the servos to hold cans.#aimant near can

📦 place_first_cans(): Moves individual servos to place the first cans.#aimant far can

📏 hold_plank(): Moves the forklift to hold a plank and activates the pump relay.(pump related)#not used

🔄 place_first_plank_and_pick_last_cans(): Moves the forklift and servos to place the first plank and pick the last cans.#forklift down

✅ place_last_cans(): Places the last cans using servo movements.#not used

🏗 place_second_plank(): Moves the lift motor and activates the valve relay.#not used

🏁 finish_building(): Resets servos and deactivates relays to complete the process.#aimant far can

❌ destroy_node(): Cleans up GPIO resources when the node shuts down.
